  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Texas received $2.2B in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 3,721 awards, with an average award size of $603K, and obligations fell 97.9% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year show large swings: FY22 totaled $70.4B, FY23 totaled $84B, FY24 totaled $61.7B, FY25 totaled $88.9B, FY26 totaled $107B, and FY27 totaled $2.2B. The Department of Veterans Affairs was the top buying agency with $884M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $641M and the Department of Energy with $285M. PANTEXAS DETERRENCE, LLC led vendors with $281M, CSI AVIATION, INC followed with $278M, and QTC MEDICAL SERVICES INC reported $246M. Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) was the largest industry by obligation with $344M, Wired Telecommunications Carriers reported $306M, and Facilities Support Services reported $285M. This snapshot covers fiscal year to date totals and reflects contract obligations only. Use these figures to compare agency concentration, vendor market share, and industry composition in Texas federal contracting so far in FY2027.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are buying in Texas right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $884M, the Department of Homeland Security obligated $641M, and the Department of Energy obligated $285M. The Department of Justice obligated $127M, and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $120M. Several smaller agencies also appear in the top list, including the Department of Transportation at $5.8M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest contractors and which industries they represent?",
        "body": "PANTEXAS DETERRENCE, LLC obligated $281M, CSI AVIATION, INC obligated $278M, and QTC MEDICAL SERVICES INC obligated $246M. Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) reported $344M, Wired Telecommunications Carriers reported $306M, and Facilities Support Services reported $285M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction obligated $275M, indicating construction and professional services are significant parts of the FY2027 to date mix."
      }
    ]
  },
